FaceAge (this repository) builds on the FaceAge release by the Artificial
Intelligence in Medicine (AIM) Program, Mass General Brigham / Harvard Medical
School:

    https://github.com/AIM-Harvard/FaceAge
    Bontempi et al., "FaceAge, a deep learning system to estimate biological
    age from face photographs to improve prognostication", Lancet Digital
    Health, 2025.

What comes from that release, and is NOT covered by this repository's MIT
license:

  - The model weights (models/faceage_model.h5). They are not stored in this
    repository; tools/install.sh downloads them from the authors' release and
    checks their sha256.
  - The numerical core of src/faceage_run.py (image loading, face detection,
    cropping and the prediction call), which is kept deliberately identical to
    the authors' src/test/predict_folder_demo.py so that results match theirs.
  - validation/reference/utk_hi-res_qa_res.csv, the authors' published output,
    used only to check this pipeline against theirs.

The AIM-Harvard release carries no open-source license. Its README states that
"the code and data of this repository are provided to promote reproducible
research. They are not intended for clinical care or commercial use." Those
terms apply to the parts listed above, and so to any use of this app: it is for
personal research use, not for clinical care and not for commercial use.

This project is independent and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
FaceAge authors.
